cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Lamina, cite it as below, together with the papers of the methods you use: Schaap & van de Weygaert
  (2000) for DTFE, Feldbrugge (2024) for PS-DTFE, and Cautun & van de Weygaert (2011) for the DTFE public software
  Lamina builds on (all listed under references).
title: "Lamina: Linear Adaptive Multi-stream Interpolation for N-body Analysis"
abstract: >-
  Two Delaunay tessellation field estimators for cosmological simulations: DTFE and the phase-space DTFE (PS-DTFE),
  which resolves the streams where the dark-matter sheet has folded. With GPU deposits (Metal, CUDA, HIP), exact cell
  averages and point evaluation, a Python package (dtfelib) and a graphical launcher.
type: software
